  "notes": {
    "raw": "\\*Entropy at 298 K estimated and data extrapolated above 670 K. \nPhase changes: 311.5 K, second order transition point of Cr; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 0$ kcal/mol.\n450 K, second order transition point of CrS; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 0$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n<table><tr><td>298.15-450 K:</td><td> $Cp^o = -29.882 + 82.496x10^{-3}T + 14.620x10^5T^{-2}$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">450-1800 K:</td><td> $H^o - H_{298}^o = -29.882x10^{-3}T + 41.248x10^{-6}T^2 - 14.620x10^2T^{-1} + 10.146$  $Cp^o = 9.210 + 3.154x10^{-3}T + 7.798x10^5T^{-2}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $H^o - H_{298}^o = 9.210x10^{-3}T + 1.577x10^{-6}T^2 - 7.798x10^2T^{-1} - 0.928$ </td></tr></table>\nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">298.15-311.5 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -35.723 - 31.246 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} + 27.021 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} - 1496.150 \\text{T}^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -35.723 + 31.246 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} \\ln \\text{T} - 27.021 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} - 748.075 \\text{T}^{-1} - 183.970 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T}$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">311.5-450 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -34.725 - 38.412 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} + 39.297 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} - 1482.550 \\text{T}^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -34.725 + 38.412 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} \\ln \\text{T} - 39.297 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} - 741.275 \\text{T}^{-1} - 224.567 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T}$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">450-1800 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -45.799 + 0.679 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} - 0.374 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} - 800.350 \\text{T}^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -45.799 - 0.679 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} \\ln \\text{T} + 0.374 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} - 400.175 \\text{T}^{-1} + 19.328 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T}$ </td></tr></table>\nSource: Data from Mills (80) who estimated entropy at 298 K and extrapolated data above 670 K. ",
